{#- Kubb: Throwing Wood's gadget (site/js/gadgets/kubb-throwing-wood-web.js): one kept match of the game on the web,
    replayed in a frame from throwingwood.com, whose /e/ pages are made to be framed (frame-ancestors *). The
    frame waits until the gadget nears the screen, and the replay inside it holds until half of it is in view, so a
    reader who never scrolls here loads nothing from that site. The link below works without the frame. #}
<div class="gadget kubb-replay" data-kubb-replay data-embed="https://throwingwood.com/e/4pqpg9bs" hidden>
  <h3>{{ thing.gadget.title }}</h3>
  <div class="kubb-replay-frame" data-kubb-replay-frame></div>
  <p class="kubb-replay-status" data-kubb-replay-status aria-live="polite" hidden></p>
  <p class="muted gadget-note">Jamie against Player 1 on the pitch a tester reported, played back throw by throw from its 110 recorded actions by the game on the web. <span data-kubb-replay-how>It plays once it is half in view, and its buttons pause it, step a throw or change the speed.</span> <a href="{{ 'https://throwingwood.com/p/4pqpg9bs' | ref('gadget') }}">Open it on throwingwood.com</a>.</p>
</div>
